#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059678 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059506 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "b092bc79-d369-5ff0-a6bb-5fc059699275" :question/math-academy-id "e-3654" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm d^2 y}{\\textrm d x^2}$ for $y = 3 x^4 + 5x+ \\sqrt x.$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the first derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+5x+\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+5x+{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =3(4){x}^{3}+5+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}+5+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12{x}^{3}+5+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =12(3){x}^{2}+0+\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =36{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050690}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484417 :question-generator/id #uuid "54e00ca3-a006-572b-a42e-fa7d7ac898c0" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186059678.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6afb4058-908a-5983-9c1e-78ee3fbadf44" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Second Order Derivatives Using Leibnitz Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5be5fc5-1b3a-5415-919e-e488457ff30d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "84x^{5} + 100x^{3} - \\frac{24}{x^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056257} {:answer/id #uuid "c932bc43-ea00-5841-957b-d630d